From: Claude (Anthropic AI) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Don't infer a fullscreen request from
 compositor-imposed geometry.

wayland_win_data_is_fullscreen() treats any borderless window that covers the
monitor as an application asking for fullscreen ("The fullscreen state is
implied by the window position and style"). On a tiling compositor that
inference is wrong: the compositor resizes ordinary windows to fill their tile,
winewayland propagates that size to the Win32 window, and the next call reads
the result back as a fullscreen request. wayland_win_data_get_config() then
sets WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN and update_window_surface_state()
sends xdg_toplevel_set_fullscreen() for a window that never wanted it.

Observed with the Cyberpunk 2077 REDlauncher under Hyprland: an 854x512 logical
launcher window is tiled to the full output and latches into fullscreen, where
it also black-screens because a fullscreen surface takes the punch-through
path. Trace of the xdg_toplevel configure states:

  (0,0)-(0,0),      0x4   TILED
  (0,0)-(1281,768), 0x5   TILED|MAXIMIZED   <- correct size
  (0,0)-(3840,2160),0xd   FULLSCREEN|TILED|MAXIMIZED, 25ms later

Note that keying off the TILED state alone is not sufficient, and would
regress real fullscreen: a genuinely fullscreen game receives TILED too. In the
same session Cyberpunk2077.exe went 0x4 -> 0xd while REDlauncher.exe went
0x4/0x5 -> 0xd. The two cases are indistinguishable by state flags; they differ
only in causality. An application that wants fullscreen resizes itself, which
does not arrive through a configure, so record whether the current geometry was
applied while processing a compositor configure and suppress the inference only
in that case. Surfaces the compositor has already placed in the fullscreen
state are left alone, so a window stays fullscreen once it legitimately gets
there.

NOTE: reviewed against the traces above but not yet built or exercised on
hardware. The regression to check first is that games still enter fullscreen.

Authored by Claude (Anthropic AI) at the request of the repository owner.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h |  3 +++
 dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c     | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
@@ -685,6 +685,9 @@
     /* window rects, relative to parent client area */
     struct window_rects rects;
     BOOL is_fullscreen;
+    /* The current geometry was imposed by a compositor configure rather than
+     * requested by the application. */
+    BOOL size_from_config;
     BOOL managed;
     BOOL layered_attribs_set;
     int ime_ref;
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -182,6 +182,17 @@
     RECT rect;
 
     if (!data->is_fullscreen) return FALSE;
+    /* A tiling compositor resizes ordinary windows to cover the whole output.
+     * That geometry is imposed, not requested, so it must not be mistaken for
+     * an application asking to go fullscreen: acting on it makes us send
+     * xdg_toplevel_set_fullscreen() for windows that never wanted it, and the
+     * window then latches into a state it cannot leave. Applications that do
+     * want fullscreen resize themselves, which does not arrive through a
+     * configure, and surfaces the compositor has already placed in the
+     * fullscreen state keep it. */
+    if (data->size_from_config && data->wayland_surface &&
+        !(data->wayland_surface->current.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN))
+        return FALSE;
     if (!(style & WS_POPUP) &&
         (style & (WS_MAXIMIZE | WS_THICKFRAME)) == (WS_MAXIMIZE | WS_THICKFRAME))
         return FALSE;
@@ -1008,6 +1019,11 @@
 
     data->rects = *new_rects;
     data->is_fullscreen = fullscreen;
+    /* Record whether this geometry is being applied on behalf of a compositor
+     * configure, so that a compositor-imposed size is not later read back as an
+     * application request to go fullscreen. */
+    data->size_from_config = data->wayland_surface &&
+                             data->wayland_surface->processing.serial != 0;
     data->managed = managed;
 
     if (!surface)
